# Avoid committing these files accidentally
package-lock.json



# Local-only 3D space GLBs, served via NEXT_PUBLIC_LOCAL_ASSETS while testing a
# re-export before it goes to R2. Cloudflare R2 is the canonical copy for every
# environment (AR-127) — a GLB committed here would bloat the repo and ship to
# Vercel, shadowing the real one. Scoped to *.glb ONLY: other files under
# public/assets (e.g. signage PNGs served from the app origin) must stay tracked.
/public/assets/**/*.glb
# FALLBACK COPY. `spaceGltfUrl` loads every space from R2 and drops to the app's
# own origin when R2 404s or cannot be reached — so a model listed here is the
# copy Vercel serves in that case. It is an exception, never a mirror: R2 stays
# canonical (AR-127), and a stale local copy left here would silently shadow a
# corrected remote one.
#
# vienna14 is here because it could not be uploaded — the R2 S3 API is
# TCP-unreachable from the office connection, its Cloudflare IP range blocked by
# the Spanish ISP. READS are fine; only writes are. Remove this line and the file
# once the upload lands.
!/public/assets/spaces/vienna/vienna14.glb

# Space bakes — the KTX2 the scene loads and the PNG sources they are encoded
# from. Same reasoning as the GLB rule above: R2 is the canonical copy for every
# environment and production ALWAYS resolves there, so committing these adds tens
# of MB to git history for files that are never served. Scoped to spaces/ on
# purpose — signage under public/assets/signs IS served from the app origin and
# must stay tracked, as must /public/basis (the KTX2 transcoder).
/public/assets/spaces/**/*.ktx2
/public/assets/spaces/**/*.png

# theprintspace branding pulled down for portal/packaging setup — reference
# material for configuring the print provider's account, not app assets.
/tps-logo-wordmark.png
/tps-monogram.png

